<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wimoweh (the Weavers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1951</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as, same melody with the chorus misheard</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wimoweh (Karl Denver)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording of the Weavers' version</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight (the Tokens)</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as, Linda's closing notes made the new tune, with English words by George David Weiss</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vimmersvej (Flemming Jørgensen)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Danish words on the Tokens' version; re-recorded in 2003 with two of Linda's daughters for their benefit</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight (Robert John)</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1971</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><a href="/songs/the-lion-sleeps-tonight">The Lion Sleeps Tonight (Tight Fit)</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1982</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion King</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1994</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in the film; later in the 1997 stage musical</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Lion King (remake)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">a version sung by Seth Rogen and Billy Eichner</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Lion's Trail (François Verster)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">documentary about Linda and the song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">ReMastered: The Lion's Share</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">documentary</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Black Is King</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2020</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the original recording used in the film, partly inspired by Linda's story</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Graceland (Paul Simon)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1986</span><span class="sg-chain-h">named as an example of the doors the song opened for isicathamiya abroad</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Marabi harmonic cycle</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">20th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the song's chord progression borrows from it</span></li></ul></section>
